label chapter_four:

    scene bg classroom
    with fade

    narrator "The pre-board exam is in six weeks."
    narrator "You know this because you've has a countdown in your planner since week one."
    narrator "You've aleays had countdowns."
    narrator "Deadlines make you feel safe."
    narrator "Deadlines mean there's a finish line."
    narrator "And at the finish line.. there's a rank."
    narrator "And the rank tells you where to stand."
    narrator "And knowing where you stand means you exist."

    narrator "You've never explained that logic before."

    thought "You're just studying."

    thought "Orion would have started his revision schedule already."
    thought "He probably started it the day the syllabus was issued."
    
    jump chapter_four_session

label chapter_four_session:
    scene bg classroom
    with fade

    narrator "Tuesday."

    orion "You've already done this chapter."

    mc "I'm reviewing."

    orion "You reviewed it last Thursday."

    mc "I'm reviewing it again."

    orion "Why?"

    mc "Knowing it and being certain of it are different things."

    orion "When did you last do something that wasn't studying or preparing to study?"

    mc "That's not relevant."

    orion "I'm asking anyway."

    mc "I read."

    orion "Phyics?"

    mc "..."

    orion "When did you last do something that had nothing to do with performance?"

    mc "I don't know what you mean."

    orion "Yes you do."

    mc "I like being good at things."

    orion "That's not the same as liking things."

    mc "For some people, it is."

    orion "Is it for you?"

    narrator "You look at your notes."
    narrator "Three pages."
    narrator "Perfect handwriting."
    narrator "Written in his style noe."
    narrator "You switched to his style two sessions ago."
    narrator "He probably noticed."

    mc "Can we just.."

    orion "Do you even like Physics?"

    mc "I don't know."

    mc "I don't know if I like it."
    mc "I know that I'm good at it."
    mc "I know it matters."
    mc "I know that when I score well people look at me differently."
    mc "I know that when I score well I feel like I.."

    narrator "You stop."

    orion "Like you what?"

    mc "Like I'm allowed to take up space."

    narrator "You didn't mean to say that."
    narrator "You've never said that to anyone."
    narrator "You've barely said it yourself."

    narrator "The library is very quiet."

    orion "..."

    orion "That's not what Physics if for."

    mc "I know."

    orion "That's not what any of this is for."

    mc "I know."

    jump chapter_four_end

label chapter_four_end:

    scene bg school_corridor
    with fade

    narrator "You walk out at 6:30."
    narrator "Later than usual."
    narrator "Neither of you mentioned it."

    orion "For what it's worth."

    mc "What?"

    orion "The way you think about problems."
    orion "The way you get to the answer before I finish asking the question."
    orion "That's not performance."
    orion "That's actually you."

    narrator "You stand in the doorway."
    narrator "Evening light."
    narrator "The kind that makes everything look slightly unreal."

    mc "How do you know the difference?"

    orion "Because when you perform, you look at me to check if it landed."
    orion "When it's real, you forget I'm there."

    narrator "You don't say anything."
    narrator "You don't have anything to say."
    narrator "That might be a first."

    orion "See you Thursday!"

    narrator "He walks away."

    narrator "Tonight you just stand there."
    narrator "Without writing it down."
    narrator "Just for a minute."
    narrator "Just this once."
    narrator "It's harder than it sounds."

jump endings